  "schoolyard_use_notes": "This tree features clusters of tiny, blue flowers that bloom in spring, providing a vibrant display and attracting pollinators like bees and butterflies. Its evergreen leaves can be used to discuss adaptations to drought conditions. The dense foliage offers opportunities to explore the importance of native plants in local ecosystems. The tree&#x27;s ability to fix nitrogen in the soil can be incorporated into lessons on nutrient cycles and soil health.",
